domain CompactV2Replay:
  description "Bounded real-provider verification of commit f1ff977"
problem P1:
  |
    Determine whether actual xAI responses work with the implemented Compact V2
    separation and ordinary and intentionally repetitive synthetic characters.
evidence E1:
  |
    The owner explicitly requested execution after the description of paid
    provider replay. HEAD is f1ff97735e7bfd42be4c21a0e421bec334052005.
    The branch has 15 unique commits and origin main has 4. GitHub main was
    read as 1cdf21009dbb8f4099dbb9ca70760320c50be6aa. No integration is required
    to test the exact implementation. One unrelated untracked v2 review remains.
evidence E2:
  |
    Source exposes protected chatJson in OpenAiCompatibleProvider. Its public
    psyche and expression methods build real prompts and decode actual results.
    advanceCharacterAgents owns V2 projection and canonical utterance acceptance.
    Existing tests build synthetic battle states without remote database use.
evidence E3:
  |
    The existing xAI fast model default is grok-4.3. Official model documentation
    read this turn lists input USD 1.25 and output USD 2.50 per million tokens
    and supports reasoning none. Repository secdat injection preflight confirms
    XAI_API_KEY exists without reading its value. Worktime ends at 23:30 JST.
premise P2:
  |
    A small replay subclass may override only transport to impose completion,
    request count and monetary limits, persist evidence and disable retries.
    Production prompts, decoders, projections and acceptance remain executed.
    This tests in-memory character stages, not deployed configuration or DB save.
premise P3:
  |
    Six sequential synthetic character turns across two characters can expose
    integration failures but cannot establish statistical quality improvement or
    prove the model's internal interpretation. Equal text is valid, not a failure.
decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, P2, P3:
  |
    Reuse the existing worktree and perform at most twelve physical requests:
    deep psyche then expression, three turns for each of two synthetic profiles.
    Use xAI grok-4.3 at the real prompt temperatures, reasoning none, JSON object.
    Each input may be at most 20000 UTF8 bytes plus 1024 framing token allowance,
    output at most 1200 tokens for psyche and 400 for expression.
    Reserve each input and output worst-case cost before sending, cap aggregate
    reserved cost at USD 0.50 and aggregate token allowance at 300000.
    Use serial requests and original phase deadlines, stop on any transport,
    decode, unexpected model, missing usage, or application fallback failure.
    Do not retry, replace failed responses, or call a judge.
    Save synthetic requests and responses locally; record the actual count,
    usage, contract checks and limitations. No deployment or production writes.

evidence E4:
  |
    Before any paid request or harness implementation, the owner deferred this
    work until tomorrow and requested handoff, WIP commit and push.

decision D2 based_on D1, E4:
  |
    D1 is retained preparation only. Do not execute the replay today.
    Preserve it with the handoff and recheck current inputs when work resumes.
